    "An SEO qualifier or alias route cannot override a literal native H1 when the current detail itself links to the exact captured pricing PDF, the entire remaining card name matches, the issuer prefix matches its official hostname, and captured SEO corroborates every H1 token. Discovery metadata alone, a missing current link or another card cannot supply identity. "
    "A single-card Pricing Information Disclosure PDF requires its literal named card, complete purchase range/variable basis, grace rule and every nonempty continuation page. Preserve the full calculation, dated Prime Rate, default consequences and application conditions; reject missing pages, competing identities and unresolved references. An issuer prefix may match the exact official hostname only when the full remaining product name agrees; never donate a sibling card's terms. "
    "A named literal Pricing Details block retains every paragraph, including purchase APR range, variable/creditworthiness basis, default triggers, transfer terms and new-cardmember approval conditions. Unpopulated DOM price bindings are acquisition leads only. An independently labelled unconditional annual fee remains separate; conflicting/qualified fee restatements still reject. "
